Let $O = (0,0,1)$ be the center of the sphere, and let $X = (x,y,0)$ be a point on the boundary of the shadow.  Since $X$ is on the boundary, $\overline{PX}$ is tangent to the sphere; let $T$ be the point of tangency.  Note that $\angle PTO = 90^\circ.$  Also, lengths $OP$ and $OT$ are fixed, so $\angle OPT = \angle OPX$ is constant for all points $X$ on the boundary.

[asy]
import three;
import solids;

size(250);
currentprojection = perspective(6,3,2);

triple O = (0,0,1), P = (0,-1,2), X = (3, 3^2/4 - 1, 0), T = P + dot(O - P, X - P)/dot(X - P,X - P)*(X - P);
real x;

path3 shadow = (-1,1/4 - 1,0);

for (x = -1; x <= 3.1; x = x + 0.1) {
  shadow = shadow--(x,x^2/4 - 1,0);
}

draw(surface(shadow--(3,9/4 - 1,0)--(3,3,0)--(-1,3,0)--(-1,1/4 - 1,0)--cycle),gray(0.8),nolight);
draw((3,0,0)--(-2,0,0));
draw((0,3,0)--(0,-1.5,0));
draw(shadow);
draw(shift((0,0,1))*surface(sphere(1)),gray(0.8));
draw(O--P,dashed + red);
draw(P--X,red);
draw(O--T,dashed + red);

dot("$O$", O, SE, white);
dot("$P$", P, NW);
dot("$X$", X, S);
dot(T, red);
label("$T$", T, W);
[/asy]

